Missing: a request that parses the whole project

The test drives `c-xref -create2`, which does not exist. What it waits for is not a
mode but a request - call it `-parse-all` - that parses every compilation unit the
project scan found and has not parsed yet.

test_ffmpeg and test_systemd need exactly that and fake it today: they search for
`non_existant_to_force_parse_all` and answer the parse-all question with
`-continue`. A search designed to match nothing is the shape of a missing request.

ADR-0024 proposed CreateMode as a standalone batch mode, and its own update of
2026-09-19 already narrows it: the XrefMode-unblock rationale is gone, and what is
left is priming and a CI entry point. With the request in place, a batch command is
a shell around it - start, -getproject, -parse-all, save, exit - which is a
convenience for a command line, not a second engine. The ADR is still Proposed, so
it can be narrowed rather than superseded.

Settle the spelling before implementing. This directory's Makefile still says
-create2 and describes driving `options.serverOperation = OP_CREATE`, which is
already an operation rather than a mode - the plan was closer to this than the name
suggested. Remove this file in the same commit as the fix.
